      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star%2C_Idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1917 a cheese factory opened in Star, later becoming the Mutual Creamery that still processes dairy today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.staridaho.org/1369/History-of-Star"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The electric railroad ran from Boise to Caldwell via Star, looping back through Nampa and Meridian in the early 20th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.staridaho.org/1369/History-of-Star"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A ditch that later extended to Middleton Mill turned dry Boise Valley land into productive farmland, drawing more settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Star,_Idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community’s early stagecoach line followed Old Valley Road to Gray’s Station, then branched northwest through sagebrush to Willow Creek Stage Station.",
